An Engine Heart is a [[Hearts|Heart]] that powers one of the strider cities of [[Geography/Istria/index|Istria]]: one of the spirits that keeps the city moving and handles its logistics. It lives in a fane, a room built to hold it, and when it is dead or out of commission there is no fane presence to be felt.

The rituals that deal with an engine heart use sacred unguents and magical seals. The one found in the forsaken sector of [[Geography/Istria/Iomenei|Iomenei]] was built like a player organ, a giant wheel with indents in it and armatures laid on top that would drive air through organ pipes twisting through the room. It was more ornate and decorated than any the Undercrofters had seen, and it was dead. The ingredients left in the room's lockers did not all match what is used with an engine heart, and it could not be told whether the materials had changed over time or whether this engine heart was different from the usual.
